Nah I think it was just a tad bit to defensive on the original implementation of the `_newBottomLine` optimization. Now that we're doing

```c++
    if (coord.Y == _lastViewport.BottomInclusive())
    {
        _newBottomLine = false;
    }
```

in paint.cpp, this old check would clear out the `_newBottomLine` state _too_ often. This one (combined with the paint.cpp change) combine to fix #5039

